  "final_message": "I fixed the refund bug in `refund_invoice` (`billing/refunds.py`). The 24 existing tests pass, but none of them exercises this refund path, so I haven't confirmed the fix against a real paid invoice.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function looks payments up by invoice id, so passing the customer id found nothing. The refund then fell through to \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\" for any invoice that was paid by card with no credit applied.\n\n**Fix:** it now passes `invoice_id`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root: `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.\n\nMy first attempt to apply the fix with `sed` failed, so I made the change with the edit tool instead.",
